// Regression (silent-class-inventory D391, closed by RUNG N): TWO owner literals sharing a
// field-name set and disagreeing about the NESTED layout each get their OWN anonymous row.
//
// This file used to be an `@emit-error` pin asserting the opposite — that the pair must keep
// taking the union box — because the alternative on offer was a SILENT one. That framing was
// half right. The pair must not COLLAPSE onto one row; it never had to stay a loud reject.
//
// THE DEFECT WAS A CIRCULARITY, NOT A MISSING DISCRIMINATOR. `anonValueFitsField` has always
// refused to merge two same-fieldset literals whose code-15 field points at different targets
// (its `vc == 15 && anonRow` arm). It can only refute when BOTH target names are known, and a
// target name is `sNames[structIndexOfObj(inner)]` — "" for a nested literal with no row yet.
// In node order `p`'s nested got a row, `p`'s owner recorded it, and then `q`'s nested was
// SKIPPED, because `anonNestNeedsRow` asks `structIndexOfObj(ow) >= 0` of `q`'s owner and that
// owner already matched `p`'s row — leniently, precisely because `q`'s nested had no name yet.
// The circle closed on itself and `q` built `(struct.new $uBox …)` into a `(ref null $anon0)`.
//
// `anonNestPolyPremint` breaks it with ORDER: the nested rows of a polymorphic owner field set
// are minted BEFORE any owner row exists, so both target names are known when the owner scan
// runs and the existing code-15 arm separates them. Measured — with no union declared at all
// the two owners ALREADY got separate rows on every compiler; the union case differed only in
// that the arm-claimed nested literals were minted late.
//
// THE READS ARE THE GUARD. `p.r.c2` and `q.r.s2` only lower if each owner has its own row: a
// collapse types one of them through the other's nested struct, which is invalid wasm, and the
// harness catches that as a module that will not instantiate. The old fixture asserted a
// message and so could not see a wrong LAYOUT at all.
//
// The 16 census-block-D cells kept in `scripts/silent-sweep/distilled/named/` under
// `d179-anonrow-price` are the MAP-container form of this shape. They stay loud emit rejects
// here — their remaining blocker is the map-value rep layer (one mv slot cannot hold two owner
// reps), which is D207's row, not this one.
type Cir2 = { c2: i32 }
type Sq2 = { s2: i32 }
type Shape2 = Cir2 | Sq2
const p = { r: { c2: 1 } }
const q = { r: { s2: 2 } }
print(p.r.c2)
print(q.r.s2)
